Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: pcwebadb
Upstream-Contact: WorkBuddy <workbuddy@localhost>
Source: https://github.com/sky22333/skyadb (design/feature reference)
Comment:
 PC Web ADB (PWA) is a NEW, independent Go/Web implementation for Linux desktops.
 Its feature list, screen organisation and Chinese UI wording follow the
 GPL-3.0 Android application "sky adb" (github.com/sky22333/skyadb,
 main @ bbf01698880f3b09c40dd0672b297fe16fd70ef6, retrieved 2026-11-14).
 No Kotlin/Java source, no Kadb code, no MIUIX code and no scrcpy-server
 binary from the upstream project is compiled into or shipped with this
 package. The upstream snapshot is kept in the source tree under
 reference/skyadb/ solely as a documented design reference.
 .
 Because the work is a functional adaptation of a GPL-3.0 program, the
 adaptation itself is released under GPL-3.0-or-later. The complete
 corresponding source of the shipped binaries is included as
 /usr/share/doc/pcwebadb/source.tar.gz.
 .
 The bundled `adb` binary is an unmodified copy from Google's Android SDK
 Platform Tools 37.0.1. It is a separate, independently licensed program
 distributed as an AGGREGATE alongside the GPL work (not a derivative work
 of it); its own licence text is preserved in
 /usr/share/doc/pcwebadb/NOTICE.txt. Apache-2.0 is GPLv3-compatible.
 .
 The Linux desktop window uses GTK3 and WebKitGTK from the host system.
 These libraries are NOT shipped in this package and are NOT linked at
 build time: the program resolves them with dlopen()/dlsym() at runtime
 and falls back to a standalone browser window when they are unavailable.
 Only libc/libdl/libpthread/libresolv are linked into the binary.
 .
 The application icons (packaging/pcwebadb-tray.png and
 packaging/windows/pcwebadb.ico) are generated procedurally by
 packaging/windows/make-icon.py from original geometry; no third-party
 artwork is incorporated. They are covered by the GPL-3+ grant below.

